    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occulco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obc-</span></b> ), āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. a.
		obcalco. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to tread</i> or <i>trample down</i>
			(mostly ante-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bene occulcato,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 49, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(cohors) occulcata pedibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 13, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 27, 14, 7</span></i> Drak. <i>N.
				cr.</i></div>
